  "description": "Listed Building Consent for the erection of a single-storey rear extension; reinstatement of original fireplace and cornicing; installation of a conservation-style rooflight to match the neighbouring property; and minor alterations to front garden hard landscaping.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this consent.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of Section 18(a) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990 as amended.\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: small;&quot;&gt;Before work begins, a minimum of 0.5 metre square sample repointing panel shall be prepared showing the proposed joints, mortar mix, profile, and finish. This shall be approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The works shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with the approved details.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: small;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Reason:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;To ensure special regard is paid to protecting the architectural and historic interest and integrity of the listed building under Sections 16 and 66 of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990 and National Planning Policy Framework, December 2024, Paragraphs 202 to 221; The London Plan 2021, Policy HC1 Heritage conservation and growth; and Hackney Local Plan 2033, Policies LP1 Design Quality and Local Character and LP3 Designated Heritage Assets&lt;/p&gt;",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>"
  ],
